-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, "Hurt" (ss 319-338).
--
-- Covers: s 319 (hurt), s 320 (grievous hurt), s 321 (voluntarily causing
-- hurt), s 322 (voluntarily causing grievous hurt), and the punishing sections
-- ss 323, 323A, 324, 325, 326, 327, 328, 329, 330, 331, 332, 333, 334, 334A,
-- 335, 335B, 336, 337 and 338. s 335A is deferred (notes/body-a-coverage.md).
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026 (inputs/PC1871.txt, lines 7170-7520 or so).
--
-- Two facts records, because the Code has two families here:
--
--   `Hurt Facts`        ss 319-335: an act done with intention or knowledge of
--                       hurt (s 321), which the punishing sections aggravate
--                       (grievous hurt, dangerous means, purpose, public
--                       servant) or mitigate (provocation).
--   `Rash Act Facts`    ss 335B-338, and s 304A in pc-body-a-life.l4: an act
--                       done rashly or negligently, measured by its result.
--
-- What a reader must know before reading:
--
-- * Every "except in the case provided for by section N" (ss 323, 324, 325,
--   326) is encoded as a NOT over section N's own ladder, so that exactly one
--   of the overlapping punishing sections frames. See body-a-forks.md F-3.
-- * s 322 and s 323A turn on the hurt the accused AIMED AT, which is a
--   different fact from the hurt he CAUSED. They are two leaves each, both
--   positive, never one leaf and its NOT: schema completion fills an unknown
--   leaf with FALSE, and NOT of an unknown must not assert a fact (F-2).
-- * The field names differ from the reference row's hurt-321-323A.l4
--   (`cause hurt`, `not grievous`, `grievous`): here each is the Code's words.
--   The catalogue entry for s 323A must be re-pointed at integration.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`

§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, Hurt (ss 319-338)`

§§ `The facts of one act of hurt`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 319-335 - the operative atoms; CPC 2010 ss 124-125 for the particulars
DECLARE `Hurt Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person hurt, as it is to appear in the charge - for example "Lam Mian Sern"
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes the person hurt, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by punching the said Z once on the face"
    -- s 319 and its Explanation
    `caused bodily pain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause the victim bodily pain? It need not be serious (s 319).
    `caused disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause the victim a disease? (s 319)
    `caused infirmity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause the victim an infirmity? (s 319)
    `caused the victim to be unconscious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause the victim to be unconscious? (s 319 Explanation)
    -- s 321 - fault elements
    `intention of causing hurt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused do the act with the intention of thereby causing hurt to any person? (s 321)
    `knowledge of being likely to cause hurt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused do the act knowing that he was likely thereby to cause hurt to any person? (s 321)
    -- s 320 - the kinds of hurt the act actually caused
    `the hurt caused is emasculation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the hurt caused emasculation? (s 320(a))
    `the hurt caused is death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the hurt cause death? (s 320(aa))
    `the hurt caused is permanent privation of the sight of either eye` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the victim permanently lose the sight of either eye? (s 320(b))
    `the hurt caused is permanent privation of the hearing of either ear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the victim permanently lose the hearing of either ear? (s 320(c))
    `the hurt caused is privation of any member or joint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the victim lose any member or joint? (s 320(d))
    `the hurt caused is destruction or permanent impairing of the powers of any member or joint` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the powers of any member or joint destroyed or permanently impaired? (s 320(e))
    `the hurt caused is permanent disfiguration of the head or face` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim's head or face permanently disfigured? (s 320(f))
    `the hurt caused is fracture or dislocation of a bone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the victim suffer a fracture or dislocation of a bone? (s 320(g))
    `the hurt caused endangers life` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the hurt endanger the victim's life? (s 320(h))
    `the hurt caused the sufferer to be in severe bodily pain during the space of 20 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim in severe bodily pain for 20 days? (s 320(h); see the helper `lasts the space of 20 days`)
    `the hurt caused the sufferer to be unable to follow his ordinary pursuits during the space of 20 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the victim unable to follow his ordinary pursuits for 20 days? (s 320(h))
    `the hurt caused is penetration of the vagina or anus without consent which causes severe bodily pain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the hurt a penetration of the victim's vagina or anus without consent, causing severe bodily pain? (s 320(i))
    -- ss 322, 323A - the hurt AIMED AT
    `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused intend, or know himself likely, to cause grievous hurt of some kind (not necessarily the kind he caused)? (s 322 and its Explanation)
    `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: was the hurt the accused intended, or knew himself likely, to cause LESS than grievous hurt? (s 323A; s 334A)
    -- ss 324, 326 - dangerous weapons or means
    `by means of any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the hurt caused by means of an instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting? (ss 324, 326)
    `by means of any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it caused by means of an instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death? (ss 324, 326)
    `by means of fire or any heated substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it caused by means of fire or a heated substance? (ss 324, 326)
    `by means of any poison or any corrosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it caused by means of a poison or a corrosive substance? (ss 324, 326)
    `by means of any explosive substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it caused by means of an explosive substance? (ss 324, 326)
    `by means of any substance which it is harmful to the human body to inhale, to swallow, or to receive into the blood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it caused by means of a substance harmful to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood? (ss 324, 326)
    `by means of any animal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it caused by means of an animal? (ss 324, 326)
    -- ss 327, 329 - extortion of property; constraint to an illegal act
    `for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer, or from any person interested in the sufferer, any property or valuable security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the hurt caused to extort property or a valuable security (s 30) from the victim or someone interested in the victim? (ss 327, 329)
    `for the purpose of constraining the sufferer, or any person interested in the sufferer, to do anything which is illegal or which may facilitate the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it caused to constrain the victim, or someone interested in the victim, to do something illegal (s 43) or that may facilitate an offence? (ss 327, 329)
    -- ss 330, 331 - confession; restoration of property
    `for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer, or from any person interested in the sufferer, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the hurt caused to extort a confession, or information that may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct? (ss 330, 331)
    `for the purpose of constraining the sufferer, or any person interested in the sufferer, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it caused to constrain the victim or someone interested in the victim to restore property, satisfy a claim or demand, or give information leading to restoration of property? (ss 330, 331)
    -- s 328
    `administers to, or causes to be taken by, any person any poison or any stupefying or intoxicating substance, or any substance which is harmful to the human body to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused administer to the victim, or cause the victim to take, a poison, a stupefying or intoxicating substance, or a substance harmful to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood? (s 328)
    `with intent to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused do so intending to commit, or to facilitate, an offence? (s 328)
    -- ss 332, 333
    `the sufferer is a public servant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the victim a public servant within section 21? (drill-down: `public servant within section 21`)
    `in the discharge of his duty as such public servant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the hurt caused while the victim was discharging his duty as a public servant? (ss 332, 333)
    `with intent to prevent or deter that person or any other public servant from discharging his duty as such public servant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: was the hurt caused intending to prevent or deter the victim, or another public servant, from discharging his duty? (ss 332, 333)
    `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the hurt caused because of something the victim did or tried to do in the lawful discharge of his duty? (ss 332, 333)
    -- ss 334, 334A, 335
    `on grave and sudden provocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act on grave and sudden provocation given by the victim? A question of fact (s 300 Exception 1 Explanations 1 and 2, applied by s 335 Explanation).
    `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: was the hurt the accused intended or foresaw confined to the person who provoked him? (ss 334, 334A)
    `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause grievous hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: was any grievous hurt the accused intended or foresaw confined to the person who provoked him? (s 335)
    `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for doing harm to any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provocation NOT sought or voluntarily provoked by the accused as an excuse for doing harm? (s 300 Exception 1 proviso (a), applied by s 335 Explanation)
    `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused neither know nor have reason to believe (s 26) that the provocation was given by something done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant lawfully exercising his powers? (s 300 Exception 1 proviso (b))
    `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the provocation NOT given by something done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence? (s 300 Exception 1 proviso (c))

§§ `s 319 - hurt`

-- 319. Whoever causes bodily pain, disease or infirmity to any person is said
--      to cause hurt.
--      Explanation.-A person is said to cause hurt if he causes another person
--      to be unconscious.
@export Whether the accused "causes hurt" within section 319 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the act caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `causes hurt` f IF
        "Whoever causes"
    ... (    f's `caused bodily pain`
         OR  f's `caused disease`
         OR  f's `caused infirmity`
         OR  f's `caused the victim to be unconscious` )
    ... "to any person is said to cause hurt (s 319 and its Explanation)"

§§ `s 320 - grievous hurt`

-- 320. The following kinds of hurt only are designated as "grievous":
--   (a) emasculation; (aa) death; (b) permanent privation of the sight of
--   either eye; (c) permanent privation of the hearing of either ear;
--   (d) privation of any member or joint; (e) destruction or permanent
--   impairing of the powers of any member or joint; (f) permanent
--   disfiguration of the head or face; (g) fracture or dislocation of a bone;
--   (h) any hurt which endangers life, or which causes the sufferer to be,
--   during the space of 20 days, in severe bodily pain, or unable to follow
--   his ordinary pursuits; (i) penetration of the vagina or anus, as the case
--   may be, of a person without that person's consent, which causes severe
--   bodily pain.
@export Whether the hurt the act caused is "grievous hurt" within section 320 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What kind of hurt the act caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `grievous hurt within section 320` f IF
        "The following kinds of hurt only are designated as 'grievous':"
    ... (    f's `the hurt caused is emasculation`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused is death`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused is permanent privation of the sight of either eye`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused is permanent privation of the hearing of either ear`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused is privation of any member or joint`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused is destruction or permanent impairing of the powers of any member or joint`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused is permanent disfiguration of the head or face`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused is fracture or dislocation of a bone`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused endangers life`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused the sufferer to be in severe bodily pain during the space of 20 days`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused the sufferer to be unable to follow his ordinary pursuits during the space of 20 days`
         OR  f's `the hurt caused is penetration of the vagina or anus without consent which causes severe bodily pain` )

-- s 320(h)'s threshold, over the number of days, so the boundary is tested.
@export Whether a period of the given number of days is "the space of 20 days" in section 320(h) of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN days IS A NUMBER @desc How many days the severe bodily pain, or the inability to follow ordinary pursuits, lasted
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lasts the space of 20 days` days IF days AT LEAST 20

§§ `s 321 - voluntarily causing hurt`

-- 321. Whoever does any act with the intention of thereby causing hurt to any
--      person, or with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause hurt
--      to any person, and does thereby cause hurt to any person, is said
--      "voluntarily to cause hurt".
@export Whether the accused is said "voluntarily to cause hurt" within section 321 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant or foresaw by it, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `voluntarily causes hurt` f IF
        "Whoever does any act with the"
    ... (    f's `intention of causing hurt`
         OR  f's `knowledge of being likely to cause hurt` )
    ... "to any person, and does thereby"
    ... `causes hurt` f
    ... "to any person"

§§ `s 322 - voluntarily causing grievous hurt`

-- 322. Whoever voluntarily causes hurt, if the hurt which he intends to cause
--      or knows himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt, and if the
--      hurt which he causes is grievous hurt, is said "voluntarily to cause
--      grievous hurt".
--      Explanation.-A person is not said voluntarily to cause grievous hurt
--      except when he both causes grievous hurt and intends or knows himself
--      to be likely to cause grievous hurt. But he is said voluntarily to
--      cause grievous hurt if, intending or knowing himself to be likely to
--      cause grievous hurt of one kind, he actually causes grievous hurt of
--      another kind.
@export Whether the accused is said "voluntarily to cause grievous hurt" within section 322 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant or foresaw by it, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `voluntarily causes grievous hurt` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `voluntarily causes hurt` f
    ... ", if"
    ... f's `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt`
    ... "(of any kind - Explanation), and if the hurt which he causes is"
    ... `grievous hurt within section 320` f

§§ `The words the hurt charges share`

-- "did voluntarily cause hurt to one Z[, <extra>], to wit, <manner>"
GIVEN f     IS A `Hurt Facts`
      what  IS A STRING
      extra IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the hurt recital` f what extra MEANS
    CONCAT "did ", what, " to ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), extra, ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`

-- The s 321 elements, named for a refusal (CPC s 123(5)).
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of voluntarily causing hurt not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `intention of causing hurt` OR f's `knowledge of being likely to cause hurt`) "with the intention of thereby causing hurt to any person, or with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause hurt to any person"),
        (`missing unless` (`causes hurt` f) "does thereby cause hurt (bodily pain, disease, infirmity or unconsciousness - s 319) to any person"),
        (`missing unless` (`voluntarily causes hurt` f) "the elements of section 321 taken together"))

-- The s 322 elements, named for a refusal.
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of voluntarily causing grievous hurt not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`elements of voluntarily causing hurt not made out` f),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt`) "the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt"),
        (`missing unless` (`grievous hurt within section 320` f) "the hurt which he causes is grievous hurt (s 320)"),
        (`missing unless` (`voluntarily causes grievous hurt` f) "the elements of section 322 taken together"))

-- "by means of ..." for ss 324 and 326, naming each means that holds.
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the dangerous means` f MEANS
    `joined with` " and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `by means of any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting`) "by means of an instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting"),
        (`included if` (f's `by means of any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death`) "by means of an instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death"),
        (`included if` (f's `by means of fire or any heated substance`) "by means of fire or a heated substance"),
        (`included if` (f's `by means of any poison or any corrosive substance`) "by means of a poison or a corrosive substance"),
        (`included if` (f's `by means of any explosive substance`) "by means of an explosive substance"),
        (`included if` (f's `by means of any substance which it is harmful to the human body to inhale, to swallow, or to receive into the blood`) "by means of a substance which it is harmful to the human body to inhale, to swallow, or to receive into the blood"),
        (`included if` (f's `by means of any animal`) "by means of an animal")))

§§ `ss 323-326 - the dangerous weapons or means, and the exceptions they share`

-- The means ss 324 and 326 list, word for word.
@export Whether hurt was caused "by dangerous weapons or means" as sections 324 and 326 of the Penal Code 1871 list them
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc By what means the hurt was caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `by dangerous weapons or means` f IF
        f's `by means of any instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting`
    OR  f's `by means of any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely to cause death`
    OR  f's `by means of fire or any heated substance`
    OR  f's `by means of any poison or any corrosive substance`
    OR  f's `by means of any explosive substance`
    OR  f's `by means of any substance which it is harmful to the human body to inhale, to swallow, or to receive into the blood`
    OR  f's `by means of any animal`

-- s 335 Explanation: "Sections 334, 334A and 335 are subject to the same
-- provisos as exception 1 of section 300."
@export Whether the accused acted "on grave and sudden provocation" within sections 334, 334A and 335 of the Penal Code 1871, subject to the provisos of Exception 1 to section 300
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc The provocation, and how it arose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on grave and sudden provocation, subject to the provisos of Exception 1 to section 300` f IF
        f's `on grave and sudden provocation`
    ... "subject to the provisos (s 335 Explanation):"
    ... "(a)"
    ... f's `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for doing harm to any person`
    ... "(b)"
    ... f's `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers`
    ... "(c)"
    ... f's `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence`

§§ `s 323 - punishment for voluntarily causing hurt`

-- 323. Whoever, except in the case provided for by section 323A or 334,
--      voluntarily causes hurt, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 3 years, or with fine which may extend to $5,000,
--      or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 323
`punishment prescribed by s 323` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "323"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 323 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant or foresaw by it, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 323` f IF
        "Whoever, except in the case provided for by section 323A"
    ... NOT (`offence under s 323A` f)
    ... "or 334,"
    ... NOT (`offence under s 334` f)
    ... `voluntarily causes hurt` f

@export Frame a charge under section 323 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what it caused, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 323` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "323" "voluntarily causing hurt"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 323`'s words)
        (`offence under s 323` f)
        (`the hurt recital` f "voluntarily cause hurt" "")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing hurt not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (NOT (`offence under s 323A` f)) "not the case provided for by section 323A (the hurt caused was grievous though the hurt aimed at was not - charge under section 323A)"),
                      (`missing unless` (NOT (`offence under s 334` f)) "not the case provided for by section 334 (hurt caused on grave and sudden provocation - charge under section 334)")))

§§ `s 323A - punishment for voluntarily causing hurt which causes grievous hurt`

-- 323A. Whoever voluntarily causes hurt, if the hurt which he intends to cause
--       or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous, but the hurt
--       which he actually causes is grievous, shall be punished with
--       imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine
--       which may extend to $10,000, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 323A
`punishment prescribed by s 323A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "323A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 5 years, or with fine which may extend to $10,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 60
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 323A of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt which causes grievous hurt)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant or foresaw by it, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 323A` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `voluntarily causes hurt` f
    ... ", if the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is"
    ... f's `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous`
    ... ", but the hurt which he actually causes is"
    ... `grievous hurt within section 320` f

-- The recital follows Ang Boon Han v PP [2024] SGHC 221, as the reference row
-- does: "did voluntarily cause hurt with the intention to cause hurt which is
-- not grievous, but which actually caused grievous hurt to one ...".
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the s 323A mens rea` f MEANS
    `joined with` " and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `intention of causing hurt`) "with the intention to cause hurt which is not grievous"),
        (`included if` (f's `knowledge of being likely to cause hurt`) "with the knowledge that you were likely to cause hurt which is not grievous")))

@export Frame a charge under section 323A of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt which causes grievous hurt), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what it caused, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 323A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "323A" "voluntarily causing hurt which causes grievous hurt"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 323A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 323A` f)
        (CONCAT "did voluntarily cause hurt ", (`the s 323A mens rea` f),
                ", but which actually caused grievous hurt to ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
                ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing hurt not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous`) "the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous (where the accused aimed at grievous hurt the offence is section 325, not this one)"),
                      (`missing unless` (`grievous hurt within section 320` f) "the hurt which he actually causes is grievous (s 320)")))

§§ `s 324 - voluntarily causing hurt by dangerous weapons or means`

-- 324. Whoever, except in the case provided for by section 334, voluntarily
--      causes hurt by means of any instrument for shooting, stabbing or
--      cutting, or any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely
--      to cause death, or by means of fire or any heated substance, or by means
--      of any poison or any corrosive substance, or by means of any explosive
--      substance, or by means of any substance which it is harmful to the
--      human body to inhale, to swallow, or to receive into the blood, or by
--      means of any animal, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--      which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any
--      combination of such punishments.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 324
`punishment prescribed by s 324` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "324"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with caning, or with any combination of such punishments"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `or with`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 324 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt by dangerous weapons or means)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, by what means, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 324` f IF
        "Whoever, except in the case provided for by section 334,"
    ... NOT (`offence under s 334` f)
    ... `voluntarily causes hurt` f
    ... `by dangerous weapons or means` f

@export Frame a charge under section 324 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt by dangerous weapons or means), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, by what means, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 324` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "324" "voluntarily causing hurt by dangerous weapons or means"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 324`'s words)
        (`offence under s 324` f)
        (`the hurt recital` f "voluntarily cause hurt" (CONCAT " ", `the dangerous means` f))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing hurt not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (`by dangerous weapons or means` f) "by means of an instrument for shooting, stabbing or cutting, or other dangerous weapon or means listed in section 324"),
                      (`missing unless` (NOT (`offence under s 334` f)) "not the case provided for by section 334 (hurt caused on grave and sudden provocation - charge under section 334)")))

§§ `s 325 - punishment for voluntarily causing grievous hurt`

-- 325. Whoever, except in the case provided for by section 323A, 334A or 335,
--      voluntarily causes grievous hurt, shall be punished with imprisonment
--      for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to
--      fine or to caning.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 325
`punishment prescribed by s 325` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "325"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 325 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing grievous hurt)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what he meant or foresaw by it, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 325` f IF
        "Whoever, except in the case provided for by section 323A,"
    ... NOT (`offence under s 323A` f)
    ... "334A"
    ... NOT (`offence under s 334A` f)
    ... "or 335,"
    ... NOT (`offence under s 335` f)
    ... `voluntarily causes grievous hurt` f

@export Frame a charge under section 325 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing grievous hurt), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what it caused, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 325` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "325" "voluntarily causing grievous hurt"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 325`'s words)
        (`offence under s 325` f)
        (`the hurt recital` f "voluntarily cause grievous hurt" "")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing grievous hurt not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (NOT (`offence under s 335` f)) "not the case provided for by section 335 (grievous hurt caused on grave and sudden provocation - charge under section 335)")))

