§§ `s 328 - causing hurt by means of poison, etc., with intent to commit an offence`

-- 328. Whoever administers to, or causes to be taken by, any person any poison
--      or any stupefying or intoxicating substance, or any substance which is
--      harmful to the human body to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood,
--      with intent to cause hurt to such person, or with intent to commit or
--      to facilitate the commission of an offence, or knowing it to be likely
--      that he will thereby cause hurt, shall be punished with imprisonment
--      for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to
--      fine or to caning.
--
-- The heading says "causing hurt", the enacting words do not: no hurt need be
-- caused (body-a-forks.md F-5).
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 328
`punishment prescribed by s 328` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "328"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 120
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 328 of the Penal Code 1871 (administering poison, etc., with intent to commit an offence)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused administered, and why
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 328` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND f's `administers to, or causes to be taken by, any person any poison or any stupefying or intoxicating substance, or any substance which is harmful to the human body to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood`
    AND (    f's `intention of causing hurt`
         OR  f's `with intent to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence`
         OR  f's `knowledge of being likely to cause hurt` )

GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the s 328 intent` f MEANS
    `joined with` ", or " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `intention of causing hurt`) "with intent to cause hurt to the said person"),
        (`included if` (f's `with intent to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence`) "with intent to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence"),
        (`included if` (f's `knowledge of being likely to cause hurt`) "knowing it to be likely that you would thereby cause hurt")))

@export Frame a charge under section 328 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused administered, why, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 328` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "328" "causing hurt by means of poison, etc., with intent to commit an offence"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 328`'s words)
        (`offence under s 328` f)
        (CONCAT "did administer to ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)), " a poison or a stupefying, intoxicating or harmful substance, ", (`the s 328 intent` f), ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (concat (LIST (`missing unless` (f's `administers to, or causes to be taken by, any person any poison or any stupefying or intoxicating substance, or any substance which is harmful to the human body to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood`) "administers to, or causes to be taken by, any person any poison or any stupefying, intoxicating or harmful substance"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `intention of causing hurt` OR f's `with intent to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence` OR f's `knowledge of being likely to cause hurt`) "with intent to cause hurt, or with intent to commit or facilitate an offence, or knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause hurt")))

§§ `ss 330 and 331 - to extort confession, or to compel restoration of property`

-- 330. Whoever voluntarily causes hurt for the purpose of extorting from the
--      sufferer, or from any person interested in the sufferer, any confession
--      or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or
--      misconduct, or for the purpose of constraining the sufferer, or any
--      person interested in the sufferer, to restore or to cause the
--      restoration of any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any
--      claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the
--      restoration of any property or valuable security, shall be punished
--      with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall
--      also be liable to fine or to caning.
-- 331. [the same, for grievous hurt] ... imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.

@export Whether hurt was caused for one of the purposes of sections 330 and 331 of the Penal Code 1871 (extorting a confession, or compelling restoration of property)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc Why the hurt was caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `to extort confession or to compel restoration of property` f IF
        f's `for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer, or from any person interested in the sufferer, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`
    OR  f's `for the purpose of constraining the sufferer, or any person interested in the sufferer, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security`

GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the s 330 purpose` f MEANS
    `joined with` ", and " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer, or from any person interested in the sufferer, any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`) " for the purpose of extorting a confession or information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct"),
        (`included if` (f's `for the purpose of constraining the sufferer, or any person interested in the sufferer, to restore any property or valuable security, or to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of any property or valuable security`) " for the purpose of constraining the sufferer to restore property, or to satisfy a claim or demand, or to give information which may lead to the restoration of property")))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 330
`punishment prescribed by s 330` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "330"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 330 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt to extort confession or to compel restoration of property)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, why, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 330` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `voluntarily causes hurt` f
    ... `to extort confession or to compel restoration of property` f

@export Frame a charge under section 330 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, why, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 330` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "330" "voluntarily causing hurt to extort confession or to compel restoration of property"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 330`'s words)
        (`offence under s 330` f)
        (`the hurt recital` f "voluntarily cause hurt" (`the s 330 purpose` f))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing hurt not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (`to extort confession or to compel restoration of property` f) "for the purpose of extorting a confession or information leading to detection of an offence or misconduct, or of constraining restoration of property or satisfaction of a claim")))

