§§ `ss 332 and 333 - to deter a public servant from his duty`

-- 332. Whoever voluntarily causes hurt to any person being a public servant in
--      the discharge of his duty as such public servant, or with intent to
--      prevent or deter that person or any other public servant from
--      discharging his duty as such public servant, or in consequence of
--      anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the lawful
--      discharge of his duty as such public servant, shall be punished with
--      imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be
--      liable to fine or to caning, provided that in exceptional circumstances
--      imprisonment need not be imposed.
-- 333. [the same, for grievous hurt] ... imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning.

@export Whether hurt was caused to a public servant in one of the three ways of sections 332 and 333 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc Who the victim was, and how the hurt stood to his duty
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `to a public servant in the discharge of his duty, or to deter him from it` f IF
        "to any person being a"
    AND f's `the sufferer is a public servant`
    AND (    f's `in the discharge of his duty as such public servant`
         OR  f's `with intent to prevent or deter that person or any other public servant from discharging his duty as such public servant`
         OR  f's `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant` )

GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the s 332 limb` f MEANS
    CONCAT ", a public servant, ", `joined with` ", or " (concat (LIST
        (`included if` (f's `in the discharge of his duty as such public servant`) "in the discharge of his duty as such public servant"),
        (`included if` (f's `with intent to prevent or deter that person or any other public servant from discharging his duty as such public servant`) "with intent to deter the said public servant from discharging his duty as such public servant"),
        (`included if` (f's `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant`) "in consequence of anything done by the said public servant in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant")))

GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of section 332 not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `the sufferer is a public servant`) "the person hurt is a public servant (s 21)"),
        (`missing unless` (`to a public servant in the discharge of his duty, or to deter him from it` f) "in the discharge of his duty, or with intent to prevent or deter a public servant from discharging it, or in consequence of anything done in the lawful discharge of it"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 332
`punishment prescribed by s 332` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "332"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning, provided that in exceptional circumstances imprisonment need not be imposed"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 332 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt to deter public servant from his duty)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, to whom, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 332` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `voluntarily causes hurt` f
    ... `to a public servant in the discharge of his duty, or to deter him from it` f

@export Frame a charge under section 332 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, to whom, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 332` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "332" "voluntarily causing hurt to deter public servant from his duty"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 332`'s words)
        (`offence under s 332` f)
        (`the hurt recital` f "voluntarily cause hurt" (`the s 332 limb` f))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing hurt not made out` f), (`elements of section 332 not made out` f)))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 333
`punishment prescribed by s 333` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "333"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `shall be punished with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 180
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `shall also be liable to`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `shall also be liable to`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS FALSE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 333 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing grievous hurt to deter public servant from his duty)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, to whom, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 333` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `voluntarily causes grievous hurt` f
    ... `to a public servant in the discharge of his duty, or to deter him from it` f

@export Frame a charge under section 333 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, to whom, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 333` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "333" "voluntarily causing grievous hurt to deter public servant from his duty"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 333`'s words)
        (`offence under s 333` f)
        (`the hurt recital` f "voluntarily cause grievous hurt" (`the s 332 limb` f))
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing grievous hurt not made out` f), (`elements of section 332 not made out` f)))

§§ `ss 334, 334A and 335 - hurt on grave and sudden provocation`

-- 334. Whoever voluntarily causes hurt on grave and sudden provocation, if he
--      neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any
--      person other than the person who gave the provocation, shall be punished
--      with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine
--      which may extend to $2,500, or with both.
-- 334A. Whoever voluntarily causes hurt on grave and sudden provocation, if he
--      neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any
--      person other than the person who gave the provocation and if the hurt
--      which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not
--      grievous, but the hurt which he actually causes is grievous, shall be
--      punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or
--      with fine which may extend to $7,500, or with both.
-- 335. Whoever voluntarily causes grievous hurt on grave and sudden
--      provocation, if he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to
--      cause grievous hurt to any person other than the person who gave the
--      provocation, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--      extend to 6 years, or with fine which may extend to $10,000, or with
--      both.
--      Explanation.-Sections 334, 334A and 335 are subject to the same
--      provisos as exception 1 of section 300.

GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of provocation not made out` f MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`missing unless` (f's `on grave and sudden provocation`) "on grave and sudden provocation"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse for doing harm to any person`) "the provocation is not sought or voluntarily provoked by the offender as an excuse (s 300 Exception 1 proviso (a))"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the offender did not know and had no reason to believe that the provocation was given by anything done in obedience to the law, or by a public servant in the lawful exercise of his powers`) "the provocation was not, to the offender's knowledge or reason to believe, given by anything done in obedience to the law or by a public servant lawfully exercising his powers (proviso (b))"),
        (`missing unless` (f's `the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence`) "the provocation is not given by anything done in the lawful exercise of the right of private defence (proviso (c))"))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 334
`punishment prescribed by s 334` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "334"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 334 of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt on provocation)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what provoked it, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 334` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `voluntarily causes hurt` f
    ... `on grave and sudden provocation, subject to the provisos of Exception 1 to section 300` f
    ... ", if he"
    ... f's `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`

@export Frame a charge under section 334 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what provoked it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 334` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "334" "voluntarily causing hurt on provocation"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 334`'s words)
        (`offence under s 334` f)
        (`the hurt recital` f "voluntarily cause hurt on grave and sudden provocation" "")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing hurt not made out` f),
                      (`elements of provocation not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`) "he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation")))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 334A
`punishment prescribed by s 334A` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "334A"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to $7,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 7500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 334A of the Penal Code 1871 (voluntarily causing hurt on provocation which causes grievous hurt)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what provoked it, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 334A` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `voluntarily causes hurt` f
    ... `on grave and sudden provocation, subject to the provisos of Exception 1 to section 300` f
    ... ", if he"
    ... f's `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`
    ... "and if the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is"
    ... f's `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous`
    ... ", but the hurt which he actually causes is"
    ... `grievous hurt within section 320` f

@export Frame a charge under section 334A of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what provoked it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 334A` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "334A" "voluntarily causing hurt on provocation which causes grievous hurt"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 334A`'s words)
        (`offence under s 334A` f)
        (CONCAT "did voluntarily cause hurt on grave and sudden provocation ", (`the s 323A mens rea` f),
                ", but which actually caused grievous hurt to ", (`one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)),
                ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`)
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing hurt not made out` f),
                      (`elements of provocation not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`) "he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous`) "the hurt which he intends to cause or knows himself to be likely to cause is not grievous"),
                      (`missing unless` (`grievous hurt within section 320` f) "the hurt which he actually causes is grievous (s 320)")))

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335
`punishment prescribed by s 335` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "335"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 years, or with fine which may extend to $10,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 72
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 335 of the Penal Code 1871 (causing grievous hurt on provocation)
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what provoked it, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 335` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `voluntarily causes grievous hurt` f
    ... `on grave and sudden provocation, subject to the provisos of Exception 1 to section 300` f
    ... ", if he"
    ... f's `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause grievous hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`

@export Frame a charge under section 335 of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Hurt Facts` @desc What the accused did, what provoked it, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 335` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "335" "causing grievous hurt on provocation"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 335`'s words)
        (`offence under s 335` f)
        (`the hurt recital` f "voluntarily cause grievous hurt on grave and sudden provocation" "")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of voluntarily causing grievous hurt not made out` f),
                      (`elements of provocation not made out` f),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause grievous hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`) "he neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause grievous hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation")))

§§ `s 335A - allowing neglect, physical or sexual abuse of domestic worker or vulnerable person`

-- Deferred (time): see notes/body-a-coverage.md. It needs "domestic worker",
-- "vulnerable person" and "employer's household" (ss 73(4), 74A(5)), which
-- are general-part's to define.

§ `Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 16, acts endangering life or personal safety (ss 335B-338)`

§§ `The facts of one rash or negligent act`

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 304A, 335B, 336, 337, 338 - the operative atoms
DECLARE `Rash Act Facts` HAS
    particulars IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    victim IS A STRING @desc The name of the person hurt or killed, as it is to appear in the charge; leave blank where no one was hurt (s 336, s 335B)
    `victim described as` IS A STRING @desc How the charge describes that person, after the name; leave blank if not needed
    `the manner` IS A STRING @desc What the accused did, as it is to read after "to wit," - for example "by driving motor car SBA1234A against the red light at the junction of ..."
    `does the act rashly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused act rashly - knowing there was a real risk of the effect and it being unreasonable to take it? (s 26E; drill-down `rashly in respect of an effect within section 26E(2)`)
    `does the act negligently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused act negligently - doing what a reasonable person would not do, or omitting what one would do? (s 26F; drill-down `negligently within section 26F`)
    `so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act endanger human life or the personal safety of others? (ss 335B, 336, 337, 338)
    `knowing or believing that such act is likely to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Fault element: did the accused know or believe that the act was likely to cause death? (s 335B)
    `causes hurt to any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause hurt - bodily pain, disease, infirmity or unconsciousness (s 319) - to someone? (s 337)
    `causes grievous hurt to any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause grievous hurt (s 320) to someone? (s 338)
    `causes the death of any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the act cause someone's death? (s 304A)
    `not amounting to culpable homicide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act one that does NOT amount to culpable homicide (s 299) - that is, done without intention of causing death or likely-fatal injury, and without knowledge that death was likely? (s 304A)

-- The fault the (a) and (b) limbs read. s 26F(2): negligence is also
-- established by rashness, knowledge or intention, so the negligent limb is
-- made out by a rash act too (body-a-forks.md F-6).
@export Whether the act was done "rashly" in the sense of the (a) limbs of sections 304A, 336, 337 and 338 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc The accused's state of mind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a rash act` f IF
        "in the case of a rash act"
    ... f's `does the act rashly`

@export Whether the act was done "negligently" in the sense of the (b) limbs of sections 304A, 336, 337 and 338 of the Penal Code 1871, read with section 26F(2)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc The accused's state of mind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a negligent act` f IF
        "in the case of a negligent act"
    ..  f's `does the act negligently`
    OR  "(s 26F(2): negligence is also established by rashness)"
    ..  f's `does the act rashly`

@export Whether the accused did an act "so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others" (ss 336-338 of the Penal Code 1871)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and in what state of mind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `does an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` f IF
        "Whoever does any act so"
    AND (    f's `does the act rashly`
         OR  f's `does the act negligently` )
    AND "as to endanger"
    ... f's `so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others`

GIVEN f     IS A `Rash Act Facts`
      what  IS A STRING
      extra IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`the rash recital` f what extra MEANS
    CONCAT "did ", what, extra, ", to wit, ", f's `the manner`

GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`to the victim` f MEANS
    IF f's victim EQUALS "" THEN "" ELSE CONCAT " to ", `one` (f's victim) (f's `victim described as`)

§§ `s 335B - act which endangers life or personal safety of others with knowledge or belief that it is likely to cause death`

-- 335B. Whoever does any act, that endangers human life or the personal
--       safety of others, knowing or believing that such act is likely to
--       cause death, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--       extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 335B
`punishment prescribed by s 335B` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "335B"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 84
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 335B of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and what he knew or believed of it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 335B` f IF
        "Whoever does any act, that"
    ... f's `so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others`
    ... ","
    ... f's `knowing or believing that such act is likely to cause death`

@export Frame a charge under section 335B of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 335B` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "335B" "act which endangers life or personal safety of others with knowledge or belief that it is likely to cause death"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 335B`'s words)
        (`offence under s 335B` f)
        (`the rash recital` f "an act which endangered human life or the personal safety of others, knowing or believing that such act was likely to cause death" "")
        (concat (LIST (`missing unless` (f's `so as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others`) "does any act that endangers human life or the personal safety of others"),
                      (`missing unless` (f's `knowing or believing that such act is likely to cause death`) "knowing or believing that such act is likely to cause death")))

§§ `s 336 - act which endangers life or the personal safety of others`

-- 336. Whoever does any act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life
--      or the personal safety of others, shall be punished -
--   (a) in the case of a rash act, with imprisonment for a term which may
--       extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with
--       both; or
--   (b) in the case of a negligent act, with imprisonment for a term which may
--       extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with
--       both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 336(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 336(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "336(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 336(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 336(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "336(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 months, or with fine which may extend to $1,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 3
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 336(a) of the Penal Code 1871 (a rash act endangering life or personal safety)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and in what state of mind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 336(a)` f IF
        `does an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` f
    ... `a rash act` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 336(b) of the Penal Code 1871 (a negligent act endangering life or personal safety)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and in what state of mind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 336(b)` f IF
        `does an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` f
    ... `a negligent act` f

GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`elements of endangering not made out` f MEANS
    `missing unless` (`does an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` f) "does an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others"

@export Frame a charge under section 336(a) of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 336(a)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "336(a)" "rash act which endangers life or the personal safety of others"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 336(a)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 336(a)` f)
        (`the rash recital` f "an act so rashly as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others" "")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of endangering not made out` f), (`missing unless` (`a rash act` f) "in the case of a rash act")))

@export Frame a charge under section 336(b) of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 336(b)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "336(b)" "negligent act which endangers life or the personal safety of others"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 336(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 336(b)` f)
        (`the rash recital` f "an act so negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others" "")
        (concat (LIST (`elements of endangering not made out` f), (`missing unless` (`a negligent act` f) "in the case of a negligent act")))

§§ `s 337 - causing hurt by an act which endangers life or the personal safety of others`

-- 337. Whoever causes hurt to any person by doing any act so rashly or
--      negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others,
--      shall be punished -
--   (a) in the case of a rash act, with imprisonment for a term which may
--       extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with
--       both; or
--   (b) in the case of a negligent act, with imprisonment for a term which may
--       extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with
--       both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 337(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 337(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "337(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 337(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 337(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "337(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $2,500, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 2500
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 337(a) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing hurt by a rash act endangering life)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 337(a)` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... f's `causes hurt to any person`
    ... "by doing"
    ... `does an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` f
    ... `a rash act` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 337(b) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing hurt by a negligent act endangering life)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 337(b)` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... f's `causes hurt to any person`
    ... "by doing"
    ... `does an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` f
    ... `a negligent act` f

@export Frame a charge under section 337(a) of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 337(a)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "337(a)" "causing hurt by a rash act which endangers life or the personal safety of others"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 337(a)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 337(a)` f)
        (`the rash recital` f "cause hurt" (CONCAT (`to the victim` f), " by doing an act so rashly as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others"))
        (concat (LIST (`missing unless` (f's `causes hurt to any person`) "causes hurt to any person"), (`elements of endangering not made out` f), (`missing unless` (`a rash act` f) "in the case of a rash act")))

@export Frame a charge under section 337(b) of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 337(b)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "337(b)" "causing hurt by a negligent act which endangers life or the personal safety of others"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 337(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 337(b)` f)
        (`the rash recital` f "cause hurt" (CONCAT (`to the victim` f), " by doing an act so negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others"))
        (concat (LIST (`missing unless` (f's `causes hurt to any person`) "causes hurt to any person"), (`elements of endangering not made out` f), (`missing unless` (`a negligent act` f) "in the case of a negligent act")))

§§ `s 338 - causing grievous hurt by an act which endangers life or the personal safety of others`

-- 338. Whoever causes grievous hurt to any person by doing any act so rashly or
--      negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others,
--      shall be punished -
--   (a) in the case of a rash act, with imprisonment for a term which may
--       extend to 4 years, or with fine which may extend to $10,000, or with
--       both; or
--   (b) in the case of a negligent act, with imprisonment for a term which may
--       extend to 2 years, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with
--       both.
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 338(a)
`punishment prescribed by s 338(a)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "338(a)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 4 years, or with fine which may extend to $10,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 48
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 10000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE
@ref Penal Code 1871 s 338(b)
`punishment prescribed by s 338(b)` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "338(b)"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine which may extend to $5,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 338(a) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing grievous hurt by a rash act endangering life)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 338(a)` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... f's `causes grievous hurt to any person`
    ... "by doing"
    ... `does an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` f
    ... `a rash act` f

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 338(b) of the Penal Code 1871 (causing grievous hurt by a negligent act endangering life)
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and what it caused
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 338(b)` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... f's `causes grievous hurt to any person`
    ... "by doing"
    ... `does an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others` f
    ... `a negligent act` f

@export Frame a charge under section 338(a) of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 338(a)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "338(a)" "causing grievous hurt by a rash act which endangers life or the personal safety of others"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 338(a)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 338(a)` f)
        (`the rash recital` f "cause grievous hurt" (CONCAT (`to the victim` f), " by doing an act so rashly as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others"))
        (concat (LIST (`missing unless` (f's `causes grievous hurt to any person`) "causes grievous hurt (s 320) to any person"), (`elements of endangering not made out` f), (`missing unless` (`a rash act` f) "in the case of a rash act")))

@export Frame a charge under section 338(b) of the Penal Code 1871, or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Rash Act Facts` @desc What the accused did, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 338(b)` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "338(b)" "causing grievous hurt by a negligent act which endangers life or the personal safety of others"
        (`punishment prescribed by s 338(b)`'s words)
        (`offence under s 338(b)` f)
        (`the rash recital` f "cause grievous hurt" (CONCAT (`to the victim` f), " by doing an act so negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others"))
        (concat (LIST (`missing unless` (f's `causes grievous hurt to any person`) "causes grievous hurt (s 320) to any person"), (`elements of endangering not made out` f), (`missing unless` (`a negligent act` f) "in the case of a negligent act")))
